WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:12.781
Priya Raman: Morning, Mark. Morning, Kevin. Thanks for jumping on. I know it was early out there.

2
00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:18.030
Mark Delgado: Morning, Priya. Yeah, 7:45 our time. I've got coffee, so we're good.

3
00:00:18.923 --> 00:00:25.192
Kevin Osei: Same. I've got a hard stop at 9:15, so if we can keep it tight, that'd help.

4
00:00:26.194 --> 00:00:32.592
Priya Raman: Understood. I saw the note you sent Friday, Mark. Do you want to start there?

5
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:45.199
Mark Delgado: Yeah. So the Salesforce piece is the thing. Calls are coming in fine, I can see them in the console, but they're not landing on our custom objects anymore.

6
00:00:46.409 --> 00:00:48.453
Priya Raman: When did you first notice it?

7
00:00:48.815 --> 00:01:02.090
Mark Delgado: Last Wednesday. Our scheduling team flagged that the follow-up queue was empty, which never happens. We average about 2,100 calls a week across the 38 clinics, and a good chunk of those should be creating tasks.

8
00:01:02.335 --> 00:01:11.968
Kevin Osei: And it's not all objects. Standard call records are writing. It's the custom ones, the ones we use for the nurse triage follow-ups.

9
00:01:12.403 --> 00:01:18.888
Priya Raman: Okay. Did anything change on your side recently? Sandbox work, field changes, anything like that?

10
00:01:19.954 --> 00:01:27.235
Mark Delgado: That's the thing. We had a sandbox refresh about two weeks ago, and after that the mapping had to be rebuilt.

11
00:01:27.235 --> 00:01:32.782
Mark Delgado: Our admin spent most of a day on it. Then last week it just stopped again.

12
00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:37.865
Priya Raman: So the mapping was rebuilt once, it worked, and then dropped off?

13
00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:46.043
Mark Delgado: Correct. And I don't want to rebuild it every time someone touches a picklist value. That's not sustainable.

14
00:01:47.344 --> 00:01:55.815
Priya Raman: No, it isn't. Can you tell me which objects specifically? Or I can pull the integration logs with the timestamps you gave me.

15
00:01:56.494 --> 00:02:05.007
Mark Delgado: It's the triage object and the referral object. Both custom. The referral one has a picklist we changed, added two new values for the orthopedic clinics.

16
00:02:05.347 --> 00:02:11.378
Priya Raman: Got it. And is this blocking patient outreach, or is it more of a reporting gap right now?

17
00:02:11.728 --> 00:02:20.379
Mark Delgado: It's blocking. The nurses work out of that queue. Right now they're pulling reports manually, which is eating about three hours a day across the team.

18
00:02:21.611 --> 00:02:32.323
Kevin Osei: From my side, it also means the Google Ads offline conversions are getting a thinner dataset. Not the end of the world, but I noticed the match rate dip.

19
00:02:33.564 --> 00:02:45.389
Priya Raman: Okay. Let me take this back to the integration team today. I'll need the object names, the field that changed, and a couple of call IDs that should have written but didn't.

20
00:02:45.389 --> 00:02:48.714
Priya Raman: Can you get me those by end of day?

21
00:02:49.524 --> 00:02:54.426
Mark Delgado: Yeah, I can do that. I'll pull three or four from Wednesday.

22
00:02:54.908 --> 00:03:05.098
Priya Raman: Perfect. If you email them to me, I'll open it with support and stay on it. I won't guess at a fix on this call.

23
00:03:06.047 --> 00:03:11.802
Kevin Osei: Appreciate that. While we're here, the PreSense screen pops have been solid. No issues there.

24
00:03:12.184 --> 00:03:17.808
Priya Raman: Good to hear. How are the QM scorecards landing with the new hires?

25
00:03:18.095 --> 00:03:24.447
Mark Delgado: Fine. We onboarded six schedulers this month, so the volume's up a bit. They're getting used to the scoring.

26
00:03:25.092 --> 00:03:30.235
Priya Raman: And staffing on the Genesys side, are you covered for the respiratory season?

27
00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:37.763
Mark Delgado: Mostly. We're two bodies short on the overnight shift, but that's a hiring thing, not an Invoca thing.

28
00:03:38.058 --> 00:03:43.984
Priya Raman: Understood. Anything on the renewal side you want to talk about while we're both here?

29
00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:50.423
Kevin Osei: Not today. We're good through next June as far as I know.

30
00:03:51.805 --> 00:03:58.708
Priya Raman: Right, June 2027. I'll flag it when we get closer. Let me get the Salesforce issue moving first.

31
00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:04.255
Mark Delgado: Thanks, Priya. I'll send the object names and call IDs this afternoon.

32
00:04:05.085 --> 00:04:12.527
Priya Raman: Great. And Kevin, I'll send the QBR deck by Thursday so you have time to review before the 30th.

33
00:04:12.903 --> 00:04:14.034
Kevin Osei: Perfect. Thanks, Priya.

34
00:04:14.938 --> 00:04:16.499
Priya Raman: Thanks, both. Talk soon.
